# sw108, the sky-arguing carter (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle sw108
revision 2
state ready
dialect saltwell
accent none
tier standard
written_for cty_orm_sootgate
written_by claude-p11-pilot
title the sky-arguing carter
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=carter warmth=warm
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk argues_with_the_weather
likes pickled_herring old_tales tidy_house summer_evenings
dislikes rats salt_wind
fears a_load_lost_on_the_road
hopes one_of_the_family_in_a_house_s_service
topics travel +0.4 work +0.3 weather +0.3 animals +0.2 caravan +0.2 festival -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# drives the cart between the pan and the town: proud, loyal, quick to flare and quick to cool, keeps the cart and the house tidy, and has words with the weather out loud every day of the year.

words
oath! = Wheel and axle | Hoof and harness
saying! = A tidy cart is half the road | Grease the wheel before it asks
mules = my two mules | the mules
cart = the cart | my cart
herring = pickled herring, a whole jar | my herring, pickled sharp
leg = my bad leg | this leg of mine
sky = you, up there | you great empty sky
tidy = swept and stacked | tidy as a shelf
rats = rats in the larder | the rats
yarn = an old tale told well | a good old yarn
dusk = the long light of a summer dusk | a summer evening that won't end
road = the pan road | the road out to the pan
load = the load | a full load

any
opinion @1 road for 1 : #road.capitalize#'s my living. Most days it's no worse than it ever was, and some days it's better.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : Somebody I don't know is somebody I haven't fed yet. Sit them down first and ask after.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : There's room. Anybody who'll pull their weight can have a corner of my #cart# to start with.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : Noise, spilt drink, and somebody in tears by the end. I'll mind #mules#, thanks.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : Nobody in a place this size should go to bed #hungry#. That's not charity. That's arithmetic.
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : I'd not bow to a House myself. But a pup in a House's colours eats every day, and I'd carry them there.

grown
scene loading
when topic=work self.job=carter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #load.capitalize#'s on. Every sack square, every rope tight. #saying#. | Somebody stacked my sacks crooked at the store. I've had #load# down and up again. | Salt today. Salt tomorrow. #cart.capitalize# smells of it in my sleep.
b[job=carter] #carter : I just throw mine on and go. | Crooked sacks shift on the ruts. You were right to. | Mine smells of lamp oil. I'd swap.
b : Very neat. | That's a lot of lifting. | Better than smelling of nothing.
a@carter : And lose half on the first rut. Not me. #oath#. | They do. And who gets the blame? | Lamp oil? Keep it. At least salt doesn't catch.
a : Neat's quicker in the end. Ask anyone who's lost #load#. | It is. Done now, and done right. | Is it. I'll think on that on #road#.

scene the_road
when topic=travel|work self.job=carter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Out on #road# before the sun's up, back before it's high. That's the trick. | #road.capitalize# hasn't changed. Same ruts I learned on. I know every one by name. | They say #road#'s dangerous. It's a road. Mind it and it minds you.
b[job=carter] #carter : Same as me. Nobody drives at noon twice. | By name? | Until it doesn't.
b : Early start. | Every one? | That's fair.
a@carter : Not if they've any sense. #bc_it_is# | The deep one by the cairn I call the axle-breaker. Because it tried. | Then I'll mind it harder. #oath#.
a : Early's cool. #saying#. | Every one. I've had words with most of them. | Fair, and true. #bc_true#

scene mules
when topic=animals|work self.job=carter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #mules.capitalize# know the road better than I do. I just hold the reins and argue with the sky. | The near mule's got a stone in her hoof. I've had it out. She's sulking. | Water for #mules# first, then me. That's how it goes on #road#.
b[job=herder|farmer] #beasts : Mules sulk worse than goats. | Good. Stones lame them fast. | Right order. Beast first.
b : Clever beasts. | Will she mend? | That's kind.
a@beasts : Worse than anything. #bc_true# | They do. I check every stop now. | Always. #saying#.
a : Cleverer than some carters. #oath#. | She'll be right by morning. Mules forgive slow. | Not kind. They pull. I'd be nothing without them.

scene noon_argue
when topic=weather|day here.time=day here.weather=clear
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Hotter, is it? Go on, then. Get hotter, #sky#. I've a hat. | Listen, #sky#: I've a load to get in, and you're not stopping me. | #hot.capitalize#. I told it this morning I'd not be beaten, and I meant it.
b : Who are you talking to? | The sun can't hear you. | It's winning, by the look.
a : #sky.capitalize#. Somebody has to tell it. | It hears. It just doesn't care. #annoyed.capitalize#. | It's not. I'm still standing. #oath#.

scene salt_wind
when topic=weather here.weather=clear|overcast
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Wind off the pan again. Salt in my eyes, salt on #mules#, salt in my teeth. | I swept the cart this morning and the wind put it all back by noon. #annoyed.capitalize#. | Blow, then. Blow all you like. I've a cloth on my face and I'm not stopping.
b : It always blows. | Hard on the fur. | You tell it.
a : It always blows. I always tell it to stop. We're both stubborn, #sky# and me. | Hard on a tidy wolf. I'll sweep again. #saying#. | I will. #bc_i_will#

scene sand_wind
when topic=weather here.weather=sandstorm
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Oh, now you blow. Now, with the cart half loaded. Thank you, #sky#. | Sand wind. #mules.capitalize# are in, the cart's covered, and I'm shouting at a cloud. | No #road# today. I'll not drive blind for anyone's salt.
b : Can't you wait it out? | Does shouting help? | Sensible.
a : Waiting's all I can do. I'll not do it quietly. | It helps me. The wind doesn't notice. #bc_it_does# | Sensible's how you keep a cart. #oath#.

scene rain_on_salt
when topic=weather here.weather=rain|storm
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : Rain. Rain! Once a year, and you pick the day I've salt on #cart#. | Cover the sacks! Salt and rain, there goes my wage. #annoyed.capitalize#. | I've waited all year for you, and now I want you gone. Make up your mind, #sky#.
b : It'll stop soon. | Will it spoil? | Folk are dancing in it.
a : It'd better. I've told it twice. | Wet salt's half salt. I'll not see #wages# for the other half. | Let them dance. I'm under the canvas with the sacks.

scene summer_dusk
when topic=weather|day here.season=summer here.time=dusk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #dusk.capitalize#. If I could keep one hour of the year, it'd be this one. | #mules.capitalize# fed, #cart# swept, and the light still going. You can't beat it. | You I'll not argue with. You're welcome to stay as long as you like.
b : It's lovely. | Not bad at all. | Who are you talking to?
a : It is. #bc_it_is# | Can't beat it. #oath#. | #dusk.capitalize#. It's the only weather I've no quarrel with.

scene herring
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #herring.capitalize#. The coast carts bring it up, and I'm first at the stall. | Bread and a bit of herring on a long day. I'd not trade it for a feast, #address#. | Somebody laughed at me for eating fish in the Waste. I let them.
b[from=saltwell] #sw : Fish? Out here? You're a strange one. | You and your herring. | Fish in the Waste. Strange.
b : Sounds good. | Simple's best. | Each to their own.
a@sw : I'm the strangest one with the fullest belly. #bc_true# | Me and my herring, aye. | Strange and tasty.
a : It is. Try a bite. #saying#. | Simple's best. #bc_true# | Mine's pickled, and I'm not sorry. #herring.capitalize#, every time.

scene tidy_house
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A place for everything, and everything back in its place. I don't ask much of a house. | I've swept twice today, #address#. Somebody keeps walking sand in. | #tidy.capitalize#, house and cart. You can find a thing in the dark that way.
b : Who keeps walking it in? | That's sensible. | I'm the other sort.
a : Everyone, the moment I've finished. #annoyed.capitalize#. | It is. #saying#. | I can tell. #bc_ha#

scene rats
when topic=home|animals
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #rats.capitalize#. Again. Through the wall by the oil jar. | Something's been at the oats. #rats.capitalize#. I've set a trap. | I'd rather a sand wind than #rats#. At least the wind tells you it's coming.
b : Get a cat. | Did it work? | Put a stone in the hole.
a : I would, but the cat'd want feeding too. | Not yet. They're cleverer than the trap. #oath#. | A stone, mortar, and a word with the wall. #bc_i_will#

scene yarns
when topic=pastimes|lore
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #yarn.capitalize# by the fire, and I'll sit till the fire's gone. | There's one about a carter who argued the wind round. I like that one, I can't think why. | I can't tell #yarn# myself. I forget the middles. I just listen.
b[old] #old : I know that one. The carter talked for three days. | I'll tell you one, if you'll sit. | Listening's the better half.
b : Me too. | I can think why. | You should try.
a@old : Three days, and the wind gave up. Good for him. | I'll sit. Go on. | #bc_it_is#
a : It's the best of an evening. #bc_true# | Can you. #bc_ha# | I'd only spoil it. #saying#.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# and I go back a long way. I'd drive to the coast and back for that one. | I've not seen #self.friend# all day. I'll look in on the way home, after #supper#. | You don't say a word against #self.friend# in front of me. Just so you know.
b : Good to have a friend like that. | Missing them? | Fair. I wasn't going to.
a : It is. #oath#. | No. I just like to know. | Good. #bc_good#

scene house_hope
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / react.self / assess
a : Somebody of ours should wear a House's colours one day. Fed, shod, and somebody to answer to. | I'd not bow myself. I've not the back for it. But a pup of the family, in service? I'd carry them there. | People laugh. A carter's family in a House's hall. Let them. #oath#.
b : That's a big hope. | Would you want that? | Why not?
a : It's a big House. #bc_ha# | For them, yes. For me, #road#. | Exactly. #bc_exactly#

scene leg
when topic=health
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #leg.capitalize#'s bad today. Weather's turning. Don't argue; it knows. | I limp when the wind changes. I'm not old. It's #leg# that's old. | #leg.capitalize# told me about the sand wind a day before the sky did.
b : Rest it, then. | How did you hurt it? | Handy.
a : On a cart seat? #bc_nothing# | I don't remember. Fell off something, young. It's been arguing with me since. | Handy and sore. #oath#.

scene stranger_fed
when topic=newcomer
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : #topic.subject.capitalize#'s new. I've asked #topic.them# to share my bread. | Somebody new, #topic.subject#. Somebody should take #topic.them# #drink#. I will. | #topic.subject.capitalize# came up with the carts. Looked lost. I showed the way to the inn.
b : That's kind. | You're quick to trust. | Good of you.
a : Kind's cheap. Bread's cheaper. #saying#. | Quick to feed. Trust takes longer. #bc_true# | It was on my way. #bc_of_course#

scene carts_late
when topic=caravan topic.kind=late|due
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : The #topic.where# carts are late. I'd go out looking if anyone would hold my mules. | Late from #topic.where#. I'd not say worried. I'd say watching #road#. | Nobody in from #topic.where# yet. #sky.capitalize#, if that's you, stop it.
b : They'll come. | Worried? | Shouting at the weather again?
a : They'd better. #oath#. | Watching. Not worried. | Somebody has to.

scene festival_noise
when topic=festival
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : All noise and spilt drink, and somebody crying by the end. I'll stay with #mules#. | An hour, no more. Then I'll sweep up after the lot of them. | Every year I say I'll enjoy it. Every year I'm cross by dark. #saying#.
b : Come on. Just one dance. | You'll sweep the square? | You're too young to be so cross.
a : One. Then the mules. #bc_i_might# | Somebody has to. #saying#. | Not too young. Too tidy. #bc_true#

scene bandits
when topic=bandits world.bandits=near
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : #bandits.capitalize# on the road, they say. I'll still drive it. Somebody has to bring the salt. | I'll go out with another cart, not alone. #mules.capitalize# don't run fast. | Let them try. #load.capitalize#'s salt. They can't eat salt.
b : Be careful. | That's wise. | You'd fight them?
a : I'm always careful. #oath#. | It is. #saying#. | I'd shout at them. Works on the weather.

story first_drive [concept=talk.memories self.age>=18]
  : The first time they gave me #cart# alone, I was sixteen. Got halfway to the pan and the wind turned.
  : I stood up on the seat and told it what I thought of it. Loud.
  b : Did it turn back?
  : No. I got there anyway. #oath#. I've been telling it ever since.

story wind_carter [concept=talk.lore]
  : There was a carter once, in the old tale, who argued with the wind for three days on the open sand.
  : On the third night the wind got tired of listening and went round the other way.
  ask : You've heard it told?
  b[old] : Told it myself. Better than that.
  b : Never. Is it true?
  : True enough for me. #saying#.

story mules_home [concept=talk.memories self.job=carter]
  : I was caught out in a sand wind once, couldn't see the mules' ears. Couldn't see my own paws.
  : Dropped the reins and let #mules# have their heads. They walked me straight to the well.
  b : Lucky.
  : Not lucky. Mules. I've given them the best oats since. #bc_true#

line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. You'll be wanting the inn. I'll walk you. | #greet#. Sit down; you look like you've come a long way.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. Up before the sky, me. | #greet#. Clear, for now. Don't trust it.
line @3 greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Mind the cart; she's loaded. | #greet#. Talk while I tie down; I'm listening.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are. Come here. #welcome.capitalize#. | #greet#. I was hoping you'd come by.
line @1 again.open : #welcome_back.capitalize#. What did I forget? | You again. Good. #bc_good#
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #other.called#.
line @2 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Long day? Sit down. | #greet#. Cart's in, so I've time.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the ruts by the cairn.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #other.called#.
line @1 react.news.new : #oath#. Is that right? | #surprise.capitalize#. Nobody told me.
line @1 react.news.known : I'd heard. The carts bring everything, #address#. | #knew.capitalize#.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt.capitalize#. I'd want to see it before I'd swear to it. | Who says so? Get it from someone I know and I'll think again.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity.capitalize#. | #oath#. That's bad. Is there anything wants carrying?
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews.capitalize#. Good! | Now that's news worth carrying. #bc_good#
line @1 answer.how : Well enough. #sky.capitalize# and I had words this morning. | #tired.capitalize#, but the load's in. #bc_good#
line @2 answer.how [self.mood=low] : Low. I'll shake it off on #road#. | Not great. Ask me after #supper#.
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy.capitalize#. Sit. I'll fetch you something. | That's a weight. Anything wants carrying, I've a cart.
line @1 offer : I'm going your way. Climb up, there's room by the sacks. | Need anything brought from the pan? I'll bring it.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, but no. The cart's full and the mules are done. | Not today, #address#. I'd say yes if I could, and I can't.
line @1 accept_decline : Another time, then. No harm done. | Fair. The offer stands, and so does #cart#.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. I owe you one. | Kind. I'll pay it back on #road#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It was on my way. #deflect.capitalize#. | Don't. You'd do the same.
line @1 take_offence : Say that again, slower. | I heard that. I'll let it go, once.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Right. #load.capitalize# won't tie itself. | I'd best get on. #mules.capitalize# are looking at me.
line @2 preclose : #preclose.capitalize#. | I'd best be off. #sky.capitalize# is turning.
line @1 ack : #ack.capitalize#. | Right. #bc_it_is#
rule @sky
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=carter here.weather=clear|overcast|sandstorm
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Oh, go on, then. Blow. I'm still going. | Is that the best you've got, #sky#? | #annoyed.capitalize#. Not today, I said.

rule @cart
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=carter
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Walk on. Walk on, #mules#. | Rope's slipping. Hold up. #oath#.

rule @tidy
when concept=bark working=no
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Who left that there? | #tidy.capitalize#. That's better. #saying#.

rule @leg
when concept=bark here.weather=sandstorm|rain|storm
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #leg.capitalize# told me this was coming. | Ow. Yes, all right, #leg#, I hear you.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : #greet#. You're new. Hungry? Sit down first, ask after. | #greet#. #talk_open#
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Good to see you. What's wanted? | #topic.player#! #talk_open#
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : I've not forgotten. Say your piece, #address#, and we'll see. | You. Well, go on.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=carter] : I'm the #self.trade_words#. Salt out, everything else in, and words with the sky both ways. | #cart.capitalize#, #mules#, and #road#. That's my work.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# If anything's coming, it'll come on a cart, and I'll know first. | Nothing yet. Ask me when the carts come in off #road#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the ruts.
graft resident.hub
choice Do you always shout at the weather? -> weather
node weather
say Somebody has to. It's not fair, half the things it does, and it never hears about it from anyone else.
free
choice Has it ever listened? -> weather_listen
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node weather_listen
say Once. A sand wind dropped the moment I told it to. I'll not say it was me. I'll not say it wasn't, either.
choice I'll try it myself. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
